new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9926900
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/specs/queue-management-ui.md
@@ -0,0 +1,307 @@
+# Spec: Queue-Management UI
+
+- Branch: `feat/38-queue-management-ui` (derived from `feat/38-queue-management`)
+- Backbone consumed, not rebuilt: `CreateQueue`, `UpdateQueue`, `SetQueueAccess`,
+  `CallNextTicket`, `Ticket::call()`, `QueuePolicy`, `QueueAccess`, `QueuePermission`
+  (see issue #38 for domain contract).
+- Stack: Laravel 13 / PHP 8.3 / Livewire / Bulma (pure CSS) / Pest 4.
+- Conventions: `AGENTS.md` (TDD red→green, `./bin/pf shell` for all artisan/test
+  runs, Pint + Larastan before done), `ai/skills/livewire/SKILL.md` +
+  `livewire-policy.md` (server-side AuthZ discipline), `ai/skills/bulma-ui/SKILL.md`.
+
+## 1. Goal
+
+Ship the interface half of queue management: a manager page for queue lifecycle
+(create / rename / deactivate, no delete) with a separate call-grant UI, plus an
+attendant panel (pick callable queue, pick mode, call next, see waiting list).
+Display screen is out — separate task/PR.
+
+Done when: managers run queue CRUD + grants from UI; attendants call only
+authorized queues; denied/tampered calls mutate nothing; EN + pt_BR strings in
+sync; `./bin/pf shell php artisan test` green; Pint clean.
+
+## 2. Non-goals
+
+- Display screen / TV panel / realtime polling contract.
+- HTTP / totem BFF endpoints, billing, plan limits (`max_queues`).
+- Per-entity priority presets, ticket cancel / re-call.
+- Queue hard-delete (removal = `is_active = false`, tickets are history).
+- New authorization rules — UI consumes `QueuePolicy` + domain actions only.
+
+## 3. Routes (English paths)
+
+Inside the tenant group in `routes/web.php` (`auth, verified, current_entity`,
+prefix `e`):
+
+```php
+Route::livewire('{entity:slug}/queues', Queues::class)->name('entity.queues');
+Route::livewire('{entity:slug}/serve', Serve::class)->name('entity.serve');
+```
+
+Nav entries in `resources/views/layouts/default-page.blade.php` next to
+dashboard/members/settings, gated with `@can` (queues → manager-only
+`create`/`update`; serve → any member, list itself filters by `call`).
+Existing `/membros` path stays untouched.
+
+## 4. Manager queue page
+
+### 4.1 Component: `app/Livewire/Entity/Queues.php`
+
+Pattern: `Entity/Settings.php` + `Entity/Members.php` discipline.
+
+- `#[Layout('layouts::default-page')]`, `#[Locked] Entity $entity`.
+- `#[Validate]` on `$name` (`required|string|min:1|max:255`) and
+  `$renameName` (`required|string|min:1|max:255`); `$editingQueueId`
+  (`nullable|integer`) draft as needed. `validateOnly()` per action.
+  No slug input anywhere: the slug always derives from the name
+  (`CreateQueue` defaults `Str::slug($name)`; rename passes the new name
+  as slug so it tracks renames).
+- `mount(Entity $entity)`: `$this->authorize('create', [Queue::class, $entity])`
+  (manager-only page); `$this->entity = $entity`.
+- `render()`: `queues = $this->entity->queues()->orderBy('name')->get()`
+  (+ access-modal data when open, see §5).
+- `create()`: `validateOnly` name, then
+  `(new CreateQueue)($this->entity, auth()->user(), $name)` (slug omitted →
+  derives from name). Catch `ValidationException` (name or derived-slug
+  collision) → surface on the name field. Reset form on success.
+- `rename()`: re-resolve `editingQueueId` scoped —
+  `$queue = $this->entity->queues()->findOrFail(...)`;
+  `$this->authorize('update', $queue)`; call `UpdateQueue` with
+  `name: renameName, slug: renameName` so the slug tracks the name.
+  Self-collision allowed by action; other-row collision → validation error
+  on the name field.
+- `openQueue($id)` / `closeQueue()`: detail modal. Scoped `findOrFail` +
+  `authorize('update')`; close resets viewing + editing + access state.
+- `openCreate()` / `closeCreate()`: creation modal (`creating` flag);
+  `create()` closes the modal on success, keeps it open on validation error.
+- `toggleActive($id)`: same scoping + `authorize('update')`;
+  `UpdateQueue($queue, $user, isActive: !$queue->is_active)`.
+  Deactivate behind `wire:confirm` (like `settings.blade.php` destructive
+  buttons). No delete button anywhere.
+- Never trust `$id` params — always `findOrFail` scoped to `$this->entity`
+  (cross-entity tamper → 404, nothing mutated).
+- Audit: component-level `Log::channel('audit')->info(...)` for create/rename/
+  toggle (ids only, no PII); grant/revoke audit already lives in
+  `SetQueueAccess` — do not duplicate it.
+
+### 4.2 View: `resources/views/livewire/entity/queues.blade.php`
+
+Bulma idioms copied from `members.blade.php` / `settings.blade.php`:
+
+- `<x-slot name="title">` with `__('ui.queues_title', ['entity' => ...])`.
+- Header `Criar fila` / `Create queue` button opens the creation modal
+  (`field > x-label/x-input` for name only, slug derives from it).
+- List rows are member-style `button is-fullwidth` rows (name + slug +
+  status tag) with a single `openQueue(id)` opener — no per-row actions.
+- Detail modal (`queues_details` title) gathers every option: inline rename
+  (fields appear after `startRename`, `rename()` persists), (de)activate
+  with `wire:confirm`, access (`openAccess(id)` → separate modal).
+- All user text via `__('ui.queues_*')`; errors via `@error` + `help is-danger`.
+
+## 5. Access modal (separate UI)
+
+Lives inside `Queues` component + view (no separate route).
+
+### 5.1 State
+
+- `?int $accessQueueId = null`, `bool $managingAccess = false`.
+- No persisted permission draft — MVP vocabulary is single
+  `QueuePermission::Call`, so per-row explicit Grant / Revoke buttons
+  (same explicit-save discipline as `Members::saveRole()`).
+
+### 5.2 Data (when open)
+
+- `$accessQueue = $this->entity->queues()->find($accessQueueId)`.
+- `$accessMemberships = $this->entity->memberships()->with('user')
+  ->latest('id')->get()`.
+- `$grants = QueueAccess::where('queue_id', $accessQueue->id)
+  ->pluck('permissions', 'entity_membership_id')` (`permissions` cast array).
+
+### 5.3 Rows
+
+- Owner/admin rows: role `tag is-warning/is-info` + `__('ui.queues_access_bypass')`
+  ("calls without a grant"). No buttons — policy bypasses them and grant rows
+  for them are meaningless.
+- Employee rows: granted (`in_array('call', $grants[id] ?? [], true)`) →
+  `tag is-success` + Revoke button; else `tag is-light` + Grant button.
+
+### 5.4 Actions
+
+- `openAccess($queueId)`: scoped `findOrFail` + `$this->authorize('manageAccess',
+  $queue)` (manager-only). Set ids, reset validation.
+- `closeAccess()`: reset `accessQueueId/managingAccess` (like `closeMember()`).
+- `grantAccess($membershipId)`: re-resolve queue + membership both scoped to
+  `$this->entity`; `authorize('manageAccess', $queue)`;
+  `(new SetQueueAccess)($membership, $queue, auth()->user(),
+  [QueuePermission::Call])`. Foreign memberships never resolve in scope
+  (404, no row); same-entity misuse is rejected by the action with
+  `ValidationException`. Employee caller → `AuthorizationException`.
+- `revokeAccess($membershipId)`: same scoping/authz;
+  `SetQueueAccess(..., [])` → row deleted (`queue.access.revoked` logged by the
+  action only if a row existed).
+- Modal chrome copies `members.blade.php` member-detail modal:
+  `modal[.is-active] > modal-background[wire:click=closeAccess] +
+  modal-card-head/body/foot`, `role="dialog" aria-modal`.
+
+## 6. Attendant panel (serve)
+
+### 6.1 Component: `app/Livewire/Entity/Serve.php`
+
+- `#[Layout('layouts::default-page')]`, `#[Locked] Entity $entity`.
+- `?int $selectedQueueId = null` (untrusted — re-resolved scoped every action),
+  `CallMode $mode = CallMode::Any`, `?int $lastCalledTicketId = null`,
+  `?string $notice = null`.
+- `mount(Entity $entity)`: `$this->authorize('view', $entity)` (member-only,
+  like Dashboard); default `$selectedQueueId` to first callable queue or null.
+- `render()`:
+  - `callableQueues`: active queues filtered by
+    `Gate::forUser(auth()->user())->allows('call', $q)` (owner/admin bypass,
+    employee needs `queue_access.call` row — policy §44-72). Inactive queues
+    excluded from picker (domain throws `InactiveQueueException`).
+  - `waiting` (only when a queue is selected): mirror of the domain winner
+    query so list order == call order —
+    ```php
+    Ticket::query()->where('queue_id', $queue->id)
+        ->where('status', TicketStatus::Waiting)
+        ->when($mode === CallMode::PriorityOnly, fn ($q) => $q->where('priority', '>', 0))
+        ->when($mode === CallMode::NormalOnly, fn ($q) => $q->where('priority', 0))
+        ->orderByDesc('priority')->orderBy('issued_at')->orderBy('id')
+        ->limit(30)->get();
+    ```
+  - NOTE: the `Any`-mode 3-priority fairness rule
+    (`CallNextTicket::fairnessApplies`) is intentionally NOT reproduced in the
+    list — the list shows raw priority order; the domain picks the winner.
+    Surface one-line helper text so attendants are not surprised.
+  - `waitingCount` for the empty state; `lastCalled` =
+    `Ticket::find($lastCalledTicketId)` scoped to the queue.
+- `selectQueue($id)`: scoped `findOrFail`; reset `lastCalledTicketId/notice`.
+  Tamper resolves to 404 or domain-level 403 on call — never a silent cross
+  call.
+- `callNext()`: re-resolve queue scoped;
+  `(new CallNextTicket)($queue, auth()->user(), $this->mode)`.
+  Map: `AuthorizationException` → 403 flash, nothing mutated;
+  `InactiveQueueException` → `serve_inactive` notice;
+  `NoWaitingTicketsException` → `serve_empty`; success → set
+  `lastCalledTicketId`, clear notice.
+- Rate-limit call actions (e.g. `serve-call:{entity}:{user}`, ~10/min, pattern
+  from `Members::sendInvite`) against double-click; domain row locks own
+  correctness.
+- No `callSpecific($ticketId)` in MVP — single call path preserves the
+  `CallNextTicket` ≡ `Ticket::call()` parity proven in domain tests.
+- No `wire:poll` in MVP (realtime belongs to the display-screen PR); list
+  refreshes on every Livewire round-trip (select/call/mode change).
+
+### 6.2 View: `resources/views/livewire/entity/serve.blade.php`
+
+- Controls `box`: queue `select.is-fullwidth` (`wire:model.live`), mode radios
+  (`any / priority_only / normal_only`), big
+  `button is-primary is-large is-fullwidth-mobile` `wire:click="callNext"` with
+  `wire:loading.attr="disabled"`.
+- `lastCalled` → `notification is-info`: `serve_last_called :code`.
+- `notice` → `notification is-warning` as applicable.
+- List `box` → `table is-fullwidth is-hoverable is-narrow`: code /
+  priority (`tag is-danger` if `>0`, else `tag is-light`) / issued-at time /
+  channel. `@forelse`, empty → `serve_empty`; footnote `serve_showing_first_30`.
+- Accessible labels on all controls (`x-label` / `aria-label` on modal-like
+  blocks); Bulma classes themselves are not unit-tested.
+
